{"Docs":[{"DocType":1,"IsAmended":false,"IsUpdated":false,"CompareStatus":4,"DocOrderId":148,"AmendedBy":[],"Notes":[],"Drafts":[],"ChunkGroupStartingNodeId":"PTIIMUCO_CH1GEPR","NodeDepth":2,"TitleHtml":"<div class=\"chunk-title\">Sec. 1-2. - Definitions; rules of construction.</div>","ShouldShowMiniToc":false,"Id":"PTIIMUCO_CH1GEPR_S1-2DERUCO","Title":"Sec. 1-2. - Definitions; rules of construction.","Content":"<div class=\"chunk-content\">\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               In the construction of this Code, and of all ordinances, the following rules shall\n               be observed, unless such construction would be inconsistent with the manifest intent\n               of the council:\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Assisted project. </span>\"Assisted project\" shall mean any commercial development which receives any public\n               subsidy, including but not limited to tax abatements, tax fixing agreements, public\n               bonds, public grants, and public land or easements sold or otherwise conveyed for\n               the benefit of the development for less than the appraised fair market value as determined\n               as of the date of transfer, and which shall not be located in an enterprise zone.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Bond. </span>When a bond is required, an undertaking in writing shall be sufficient.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Certified mail. </span>In all cases in the Code where the words \"registered mail\" appear they shall mean\n               \"registered or certified mail\".\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">City. </span>The words \"the city\" shall mean the City of Hartford in the County of Hartford and\n               State of Connecticut.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Commercial development. </span>\"Commercial development\" shall mean any plant, building, office building, other real\n               property improvement, or part thereof, which is newly constructed or substantially\n               renovated or expanded and which is to be used primarily for manufacturing uses; office,\n               general and professional use; service uses; and trade uses as set out in section 35-853\n               of the municipal code. A commercial development shall not include any project with\n               a gross building floor area not exceeding forty thousand (40,000) square feet nor\n               any project specifically excluded by a majority vote of the council.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Computation of time. </span>Whenever a notice is required to be given or an act to be done a certain length of\n               time before any proceeding shall be had, the day on which such notice is given or\n               such act is done shall be counted in computing the time, but the day on which such\n               proceeding is to be had shall not be counted.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Council. </span>The word \"council\" shall mean the court of common council of the City of Hartford.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">County. </span>The words \"the county\" shall mean the County of Hartford in the State of Connecticut.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Delegation of authority. </span>Whenever a provision appears requiring the head of a department or other officer of\n               the city to do some act or perform some duty, or granting some right to him as such\n               official, it shall be construed to authorize such department head or officer to designate,\n               delegate and authorize subordinates to do the required act or perform the required\n               duty, or it shall grant to them such right, unless the terms of the provision designate\n               otherwise.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Developer. </span>\"Developer\" shall mean any person, nonprofit corporation, business corporation, partnership,\n               limited partnership, joint venture, trust, association or other persons or organizations\n               having as one (1) of its or their purposes the construction, rehabilitation, ownership\n               or operation of commercial buildings.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Floor area. </span>\"Floor area\" shall have the same meaning as set out in <a href=\"\" data-chunk-id=\"PTIIMUCO_CH35ZO_S35-2LAUSREFE\" class=\"section-link\" data-product-id=\"10895\">section 35-2</a> of the Municipal Code.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Gender. </span>A word importing the masculine gender only shall extend and be applied to females\n               and to firms, partnerships and corporations as well as to males, and words importing\n               the feminine gender may apply to males.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">General statutes. </span>The words \"general statutes\" shall mean the most recent revision of the general statutes\n               of the State of Connecticut, as from time to time amended.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Joint authority. </span>Words purporting to give authority to several persons shall be construed as giving\n               such authority to a majority of such persons.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Linkage trust fund. </span>\"Linkage trust fund\" shall mean an account to collect and disburse moneys raised for\n               the purposes of such fund.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Minority. </span>\"Minority\" shall mean a person listed in one (1) of the categories defined in <a href=\"\" data-chunk-id=\"PTIIMUCO_CH2AD_ARTVIIICEPUSYOTPOPEPR_DIV2THPRPRSOAW_S2-548COSO\" class=\"section-link\" data-product-id=\"10895\">section 2-548</a>(c)(1)—(4).\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Month. </span>The word \"month\" shall mean a calendar month.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Number. </span>A word importing the singular number only may extend and be applied to several persons\n               and things as well as to one (1) person and thing, and a word importing the plural\n               number may apply to one (1) person or thing.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Oath. </span>The word \"oath\" shall be construed to include an affirmation in all cases in which\n               by law an affirmation may be substituted for an oath, and in such cases the words\n               \"swear\" and \"sworn\" shall be equivalent to the words \"affirm\" and \"affirmed.\"\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Office developer. </span>\"Office developer\" shall mean any developer of an office development.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Office developments. </span>\"Office developments\" shall mean any commercial developments, not located in a designated\n               enterprise zone, used primarily for office purposes, not including medical, educational\n               or retail use.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Owner. </span>The word \"owner,\" applied to a building or land, shall include any part owner, joint\n               owner, tenant in common, tenant in partnership, or joint tenant of the whole or of\n               a part of such building or land.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Person; another. </span>The words \"person\" and \"another\" may extend and be applied to communities, companies,\n               corporations, public or private, societies and associations.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Preceding, following. </span>The words \"preceding\" and \"following\" shall mean next before and next after, respectively.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Shall; may. </span>The word \"shall\" is held to be mandatory; \"may\" shall be held to be permissive.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Sidewalk. </span>The word \"sidewalk\" shall mean any portion of the street, usually lying on either\n               side thereof, between the curb and the adjacent street line, intended for the use\n               of pedestrians.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Signature, subscription. </span>The word \"signature\" or \"subscription\" shall include a mark when a person cannot write.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">State. </span>The word \"state\" shall mean the State of Connecticut.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Street. </span>The word \"street\" shall be construed to embrace streets, avenues, boulevards, highways,\n               roads, alleys, lanes, viaducts, bridges and the approaches thereto, and all other\n               public thoroughfares in the city and shall mean all that part thereof from street\n               line to street line of the premises abutting thereon.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Tense. </span>Words used in the past or present tense shall include the future as well as the past\n               and present.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Town. </span>The words \"the town\" shall mean the Town of Hartford, in the County of Hartford and\n               State of Connecticut.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Written, in writing. </span>The term \"written\" or \"in writing\" shall be construed to include any representation\n               of words, letters or figures, whether by printing or otherwise.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"p0\">\n               <span class=\"ital\">Year. </span>The word \"year\" shall mean a calendar year.\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"historynote0\">\n               (Code 1977, § 1-3; Ord. No. 20-86, 6-23-86; Ord. No. 30-87, 9-28-87)\n               </p>\n            <p class=\"refstatelaw0\" block_type=\"hang\"><b>State Law reference— </b>\n               Rules of construction for statutory purposes, G.S. § 1-1 et seq.\n               </p></div>","SortDate":null,"Footnotes":null}],"NewOrds":[],"PdfUrl":null,"LastOrd":null,"PrevNode":{"Id":"PTIIMUCO_CH1GEPR_S1-1HOCODECI","Heading":"Sec. 1-1. - How Code designated and cited.","NodeDepth":2,"HasChildren":false,"ParentId":"PTIIMUCO_CH1GEPR","DocOrderId":147,"Children":[],"Data":{"NodeKey":null,"IsUpdated":false,"IsAmended":false,"HasAmendedDescendant":false,"CompareStatus":4,"DocType":1,"DepthOverride":null,"ChunkGroupStartingId":null}},"NextNode":{"Id":"PTIIMUCO_CH1GEPR_S1-3LICOCO","Heading":"Sec. 1-3. - Liberal construction of Code.","NodeDepth":2,"HasChildren":false,"ParentId":"PTIIMUCO_CH1GEPR","DocOrderId":149,"Children":[],"Data":{"NodeKey":null,"IsUpdated":false,"IsAmended":false,"HasAmendedDescendant":false,"CompareStatus":4,"DocType":1,"DepthOverride":null,"ChunkGroupStartingId":null}},"ShowToc":false}